Package: islandepi
Title: Epidemiological Methods for Island Health
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Temuulen", "Enebish", , "temuulen@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides validated helpers for common applied epidemiology
    tasks, including surveillance event and feed-coverage checks, complete
    period counts, descriptive baselines and current-window summaries, age
    grouping, checked denominator joins, crude and directly standardized
    rates with published standard populations, proportions with binomial
    intervals, Poisson confidence intervals, reporting calendars, period
    comparisons, reporting-delay summaries, optional Farrington outbreak
    detection, small-cell suppression, count rounding and output
    reconciliation. It also retrieves standardized population
    denominators and health-geography boundaries from pinned BC Data Catalogue
    records. Methods are explicit and designed for reproducible public health
    analysis.
